This week has been quite a week. Mostly in the dance side of my ministry here. My dance captain, Amy, has been trying to recover from being sick most this week. She has a long awaited trip back to the states coming up next week. She stayed home and rested hoping to be better before she left. As a result she had me teach the ballet class. Yup. My second week here and I’m teaching a ballet class. It was exciting and terrifying. But I made it through alive and learned a a bi about making ballet exercise routines. This is particularly good because Amy, as I said, will be gone next week. So I have to teach this coming week as well. She is really pushing me hard.

DSCN7975Friday we had more choreography for our ministry pieces. this time it was learning the solo parts. Many of these involved lifts. Here is a picture of Amy demonstrating the jump with me. This particular time she came at me with a little more speed than normal, hence our laughing. There were a lot of jumps, and my back is really tired now.

 

Went and saw the Birmingham Royal Ballet yesterday. It was three one act ballets. The first was an analogy for energy, various ballets about things such as mass and light. A very interpretive piece with a lot of very technically difficult moves. Quite inspiring. Then there was a tribute to a late mentor. Very elegant and emotional piece. and then it finished with a piece called “The Penguin Café” which was a lot of very cheerful piece that focused on animals. I really wish I had one of the penguin hats.

The first piece is one that I’d like to talk about a little bit though. We hadn’t been given a program before the piece started. So we were left to our own devices to figure out what was going on. I took the first song in the first piece as a piece about world war two bombings. The piece however was simply entitled “Energy”. I talked to Amy about it afterwards and after explaining what I saw she could see how I picked that out. We then talked about the importance of clarity in choreography. While it is cool how the same piece could have multiple meanings, it does mean that we want to think about what we design. How can what we come up with be interpreted and is that how we want it to be interpreted?

This whole time in the dance track is really forcing me to grow as a Christian and an Artist. I look forward to what God has in store next.
